course: dictionary
lesson: 3012
title: Discs, players and streaming
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A DVD is a flat, round, shiny disc. It can hold films, music, games or computer files. The letters DVD are a short name, and the plural is DVDs with an s. «Sam put the DVD in the player and pressed play.» The clues are disc, player and play: a DVD goes in a player so you can watch a film.
explain: Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «The library lends DVDs for two weeks.» Lends means gives something for a while, so a library DVD is one you borrow and take home. Ask yourself what would fit here, then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words belong to a group, like disc, player, stream and download. «Today many people stream films instead of using a DVD.» Stream means watch a film over the internet without a disc. The sentence tells you that a DVD is one way of watching films, and streaming is another.
fact: A DVD is a flat, round, shiny disc.
fact: A DVD can hold films, music, games or computer files.
fact: A DVD is read by a DVD player or by a computer.
fact: «Stream» means watch a film over the internet, without using a disc.
fact: To find the total cost of DVDs, multiply the number of DVDs by the price of one: 3 DVDs × £4 = £12.
exercise: «Sam put the DVD in the player and pressed play.» What is a DVD? | *A flat, round, shiny disc | A small box with wheels | A kind of cloud on a computer | A type of bread
exercise: Ella buys 4 DVDs. Each DVD costs £3. What is the total cost? | £7 | £1 | £34 | *£12
exercise: «Today many people stream films instead.» What does stream mean here? | Drip slowly from a tap | *Watch a film over the internet | Dry in the sun | Swim fast in a river
test: «The library lends DVDs for two weeks.» What does lends mean here? | Throws something away | Hides something | *Gives something for a while, to be given back | Sells something forever
test: What can both a DVD player and a computer do? | *Read a DVD | Bake a cake | Fly a kite | Grow flowers
exam: Jayden says, «A DVD is just a film.» Why is he not quite right? | A DVD is always a bird | *A DVD can also hold music, games or computer files | A DVD only works in the sea | He is completely right
